  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "A bug crawls along a number line, starting at \\(-2.\\) It crawls to \\(-6,\\) then turns around and crawls to \\(5.\\) How many units does the bug crawl altogether?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9\\)",
    "B": "\\(11\\)",
    "C": "\\(13\\)",
    "D": "\\(14\\)",
    "E": "\\(15\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Add the lengths of both parts of the journey. Each length is the absolute value of the change in position, so the total distance is\n\\[\n|-6-(-2)|+|5-(-6)|\n=4+11=\\boxed{15}\n\\]\nunits. The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
